    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d62">

                <pb facs="0082" n="73" xml:id="pg73"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/513: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Sweden</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-04-11T16:00:00-05:00">April 11, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. Your 48, April 10, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="9" xml:id="d62-f1"/> and Department’s
                    62, April 10, 9 p.m. With respect to query number 3 German vessels
                    Tralleborg–Sassnitz route may be used when neutral vessels not reasonably
                    available.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
